{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli married Eschiva of Armenia and had at least three children with her including Raymond IV Count of Tripoli and Melisende of Tripoli. \n\n**Family and Succession** \nThe family of Raymond III Count of Tripoli was part of the complex web of relationships between the nobility of the Crusader states. His father Raymond II Count of Tripoli had married Hodierna of Jerusalem who was a member of the House of Anjou. \n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli had a complex relationship with his father-in-law Joscelin III Count of Edessa who had been imprisoned by Zengi in 1144. Raymond III Count of Tripoli worked to secure his release and ultimately succeeded in 1152 when Zengi was killed. \n\n**Military Campaigns** \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli played a key role in the military campaigns of the Crusader states during his reign. In 1163 he allied with King Amalric of Jerusalem to fight against the forces of Nur ad-Din the son of Zengi. \n\nThe two armies clashed at the Battle of Harim in 1164 where Raymond III Count of Tripoli led the vanguard of the Crusader forces. The battle was a disaster for the Crusaders and they were forced to retreat. \n\nIn 1177 Raymond III Count of Tripoli allied with King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem to fight against Saladin the future Sultan of Egypt. The two armies clashed at the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 where Raymond III Count of Tripoli led the vanguard of the Crusader forces. The battle was a victory for the Crusaders. \n\n**Death and Legacy** \nRaymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin where he fought alongside King Guy of Jerusalem. He was captured and eventually killed by Saladin's forces. \n\nHis death marked the end of the County of Tripoli and it was eventually absorbed into the Kingdom of Armenia.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.3748852e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00829915}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.27775657}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.483477e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.0981891}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00077872945}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.63723624}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.7335094}, {"token": " ruler", "logprob": -1.5898371}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0016219568}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.035482448}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.08053109}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -6.198691e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00024709033}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00030238825}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.54117495}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.02320934}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.0006976078}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.00064554834}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -0.21338204}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.14482976}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.007003876}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0730387}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0010718321}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -0.00055262074}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -0.0013898485}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.03063929}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.111211866}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.03648004}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.22875531}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.15249243}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0017295416}, {"token": "